<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bamenda</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bamenda is a city in the Grassfields of north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cameroon">Cameroon</a> and the capital of the North-West Region. It grew from a German military station established in the early 20th century near older Grassfields kingdoms such as Bafut, Mankon and Bali-Nyonga, and became an administrative centre of the British-ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/southern-cameroons">Southern Cameroons</a>. It is the chief city of Cameroon's English-speaking north-west.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bamenda.jpg" alt="Bamenda" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bamenda_from_mountain_road.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
